c(20, "§3.4 P2 table (verbatim); §2.4 ADHD; §7.5", "audience", "It produces a result — outcome_any 106 (42.40%, high-priority, mean 4.97) (verbatim): " + table("### P2 — It produces a result", 0) + " — OUT_MENTAL and OUT_ADHD are small but distinct: 'I struggle with my mental health … I'm grateful for the creator'; 'tenho feito para ansiedade ele tem me ajudado muito'; 'простір, де хочеться бути собою і рости без тиску й сорому' ('a space where you want to be yourself and grow without pressure or shame'); ADHD / ADD / hypersensitivity named by 5 as why the visual approach works: 'Ich (ADHS) habe schon so viel ausprobiert, sehr viel Zettelwirtschaft, Kalender, andere Apps, Checklisten, alles mögliche. Nichts hat funktioniert. Diese App macht mich froh.'; DES_GIRLY 12 (4.80%, 5.00) frame the appeal as explicitly feminine ('idealna dla dziewczyn'; 'so cute n girly'; 'КОСМОС для дівочих очей'; 'all girls should have this beautiful habit tracker'); a shift toward female / ADHD audiences (2.38% → 8.11% → 6.00%; 1.59% → 4.00%) is a hypothesis, not a trend", "aesthetic for women / ADHD", "praise", "outcome_any 106 (42.40%) 4.97; OUT_ADHD 5; OUT_MENTAL 7; DES_GIRLY 12", "none", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["12384692708","12738790672","12915261076","13636723246","12134418859","12557517143"])
c(21, "§2.4; §3.4 P5; §5.2 trigger 1; §8.4", "tactic", "The app family sells the app: ecosystem 26 (10.40%, high-priority, mean 4.88), rising 8.73% → 9.46% → 14.00% ('The family effect is strengthening, not fading'); ECO_CROSSSELL 8 came because of another app by the developer (Fleur budget, Floret planner, Nost); the listing opens 'From the makers of Fleur!': 'All the apps by this developer are so elegant, minimalist and easy to use … I encourage you all to download and start using the Habit Hearts, Floret, Fleur, Nost app'; a review titled 'If you love Fleur Budget'; 'it matches the aesthetic of the other apps by the developer so that my phone just feels like it had the prettiest makeover ever'; outcome: 3 of 12 payers bought on trust from the family — 'Yo la compré sin apenas usar la versión gratuita … ya que uso desde hace tiempo Floret … y Fleur … y estaba convencida de que no me iba a defraudar' — and the same mechanism produced the only refund request (bought on trust, disliked it); 'Cross-promotion inside the family is better evidenced here than any in-app feature'", "cross-sell 'From the makers of Fleur!'", "purchase-driver", "ecosystem 26 (10.40%) 4.88; CROSSSELL 8; 3/12 payers", "do", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["11990190046","13540828482","14506458348","12051634060","12163311892"])
c(22, "§3.4 P3, P6; §7.4 T2, T5", "insight", "Ease and competitive preference rise with time: UX_EASE 52 (20.80%, mean 4.94 — the highest-rated theme of real size) rises 15.87% → 27.03% → 24.00% (early reviews rate a first impression; later reviewers report it is also easy); COMP_BEST 24 (9.60%, 5.00) triples 5.56% → 10.81% → 18.00% and COMP_SWITCH 9 tried others first — 'the best habit tracking app I have ever used, and I have tested many'; 'Próbowałam innych aplikacji ale ta zdecydowanie jest najlepsza'; 'I've tried many habit trackers and honestly this one beats them all' — 'The people still arriving in year two are arriving having tried the alternatives'", "n/a", "praise", "UX_EASE 52 (20.80%) 4.94; COMP_BEST 5.56% → 18.00%", "none", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["14211041776","12149256614","13610326702"])
